fix(compose): land on AlbumPicker review screen w/ Next CTA after picking

Per Dan's screenshots: FB's flow after tapping a video in the picker
is to show a "Next" button which advances to the staging/edit screen.
Earlier I shortcut to step='edit' on file selection — which technically
worked but didn't surface our own "Next" button anywhere, so the user
never saw the visual confirmation step Dan pointed to.

Fix: in SharedPostCreator's handleFiles handoff (the iOS-user-gesture
path) set composeStore.step = 'picker' instead of 'edit'. AlbumPicker
mounts with media already populated, so the auto-fire useEffect is
gated (media.length > 0) and won't re-open the iOS picker. The user
sees the 3-col review grid with their selected items + numbered
selection circles + bottom thumb-strip + sticky blue "Next" button.

Tap Next → AlbumPicker.onNext = () => setStep('edit') → EditPostScreen
with preview tile, description, location, etc. (the staging area).

This matches the FB sequence Dan called out:
  iOS Photos picker → Next button → edit/staging
=======
fix(compose): MAX-RIGOR audit — chirp, broadcastSync, masterBus, co-authors, audience UX trap

Pass-1 of the maximum-rigor 4-pass audit found 4 new bugs in the
compose-V2 flow. All fixed in this commit, then Pass 2/3/4 re-run
clean.

BUG #1 (HIGH) — audio chirp missing on post success.
  SharedPostCreator's old handlePost fired a WebAudio chirp on success
  (cf. pages/hub/social-media/index.js:5430). compose.js took over the
  post-create handler and silently dropped this. Restored: 880Hz → 1320Hz
  exponential ramp on AudioContext, ~200ms total, gated try/catch so
  audio failure never blocks the post.

BUG #2 (CRITICAL) — user's own post never appeared in their own feed.
  social-media/index.js:4313 deliberately SKIPS self-authored posts on
  the realtime INSERT subscription, with the comment "already added
  optimistically in handlePost". Compose.js never adds optimistically AND
  never falls through to a feed reload — so the user posts, lands back
  on /hub/social-media, and sees the OLD feed without their fresh post
  until manual refresh.

  Fix: emit window.masterBus.publish('SOCIAL_POST', {...}) which the
  social-media page is already subscribed to (4382-4385) and triggers
  loadFeed(0). Also added broadcastSync('smarter_poker_social_sync',
  {action: 'refresh_feed', tabId: BROADCAST_TAB_ID}) so OTHER open tabs
  refresh their feeds too. Same pattern social-media/index.js handlePost
  uses on line 5247-5248.

BUG #3 (HIGH) — picking 'Specific friends' / 'Friends except…' / 'Custom'
  with no friend picker UI silently makes the post invisible to everyone
  but the author. Without a picker, audience_list stays empty;
  fn_can_view_post returns FALSE for the empty-list branches; the post
  becomes effectively 'Only me' without telling the user.

  Fix: tagged the three modes with `comingSoon: true` in
  VisibilityPickerSheet OPTIONS. Disabled buttons render with 'COMING SOON'
  badge + opacity 0.5 + cursor not-allowed. The mode switcher remains
  visible (UI hint to the user) but un-tappable. The two functional
  modes ('Public', 'Friends', 'Only me') stay enabled. The proper
  audience-list picker is Phase B follow-up work.

BUG #4 (MEDIUM) — co-authors picked in TagPeopleSheet were never persisted.
  state.coAuthors was written by the sheet but never read by handlePostNow.
  fn_create_social_post doesn't have a co-author param yet (Phase B follow-up
  schema work — needs social_post_collaborators table + invite/accept flow).
  For now, persist the picked IDs onto social_posts.metadata.co_authors so
  the data isn't lost. Same pattern as share_to_groups.

  Combined the metadata sidecar UPDATE with the share_to_groups one so we
  do a single read-merge-write instead of two round-trips. The merge
  preserves any sibling fields the RPC stored.

Pass 2/3/4 re-run results:
  • Pass 2 (real-time scenarios) — all 5 traces clean. Only finding is
    a PRE-EXISTING gap: realtime subscription on social_posts only
    listens to INSERT, so post-transcode UPDATEs (replacing media_urls
    with H.264 + setting thumbnail_url) don't propagate live. Not a
    compose-V2 regression; tracked for follow-up.
  • Pass 3 (adversarial) — clean. fn_create_social_post role/uid check
    blocks impersonation; CHECK constraint blocks invalid audience_mode;
    fn_can_view_post fails-closed on unknown mode; service-role bypass
    only available to server-side endpoints (not user JWTs).
  • Pass 4 (edge cases) — clean. inFlight gate blocks rapid Post taps;
    beforeunload protection blocks tab close mid-upload; reset() revokes
    blob URLs on unmount; AudioContext failure caught.
